# USC-II reduction: results and limits

## Result

Three useful reductions are submitted. The smallest has **81 species and 464 reactions** (27.0% fewer species and 40.8% fewer reactions), with maximum parent-reference errors of **13.84% for ignition delay and 8.21% for flame speed** across 225 conditions. Choose the 101-species/542-reaction conservative model when the stricter 10% ignition / 5% flame fidelity tier is needed; its observed maxima are 5.81% and 4.19%. The 87-species/513-reaction model supplies an intermediate trade-off.

All submitted mechanisms were designed in this run from the supplied **111-species, 784-reaction** parent. They retain complete reactions and original rate, thermodynamic and transport parameters. No existing reduced mechanism was downloaded or substituted.

Final parent comparisons cover **157 ignition cases and 68 freely propagating flames** across 15 fuel compositions and four additional blends. The 225-case pool contains 60 initial training cases, 127 original validation cases and 38 fresh confirmation cases. The original validation feedback was used to repair the smaller models; those 127 cases are not independent confirmation for the revisions. The 38 fresh cases were frozen before evaluating repairs. All final flames use finer 0.03/0.06 settings. The actual parent-fidelity cases span initial ignition temperatures 1000–1622.15 K, 1–30 atm and equivalence ratios 0.5701–1.5839; flame inlets span 300–450 K, 1–5 atm and equivalence ratios 0.65–1.4. These are sampled ranges, not a full Cartesian grid. Twelve separate toluene shock-tube observations provide an external check.

| Submitted mechanism | Species (removed) | Reactions (removed) | Ignition mean / maximum error | Flame-speed mean / maximum error | Criteria on tested cases |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| [usc2_conservative](mechanisms/usc2_conservative.yaml) | 101 (9.0%) | 542 (30.9%) | 0.82% / 5.81% | 1.15% / 4.19% | 10% ignition / 5% flame |
| [usc2_balanced_repaired](mechanisms/usc2_balanced_repaired.yaml) | 87 (21.6%) | 513 (34.6%) | 1.40% / 12.05% | 1.60% / 5.53% | 20% ignition / 10% flame |
| [usc2_compact_repaired](mechanisms/usc2_compact_repaired.yaml) | 81 (27.0%) | 464 (40.8%) | 2.11% / 13.84% | 2.07% / 8.21% | 20% ignition / 10% flame |

**Errors in this table are relative to parent predictions, not experimental errors.** The thresholds were chosen before screening: maximum 10%/5% for ignition/flame fidelity, with an exploratory 20%/10% tier. Passing a finite case set does not establish accuracy throughout a continuous operating envelope.

